# Line endings.
#
# The repo stores LF. With core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites that
# to CRLF in the working tree, which is fine for source but breaks anything
# compared BYTE FOR BYTE against a recorded baseline.
#
# That is not hypothetical: UI/WebUI/tools/webctl/flows.mjs compares its
# freshly generated snapshot (JSON.stringify -> LF) against the baseline file
# read off disk (CRLF after checkout), so every flow failed on Windows with a
# diff whose two sides were character-for-character identical. The suite has
# never been runnable there.
#
# Default: let git decide for text, as before.
* text=auto

# Recorded baselines and fixtures: byte artifacts, never converted. A snapshot
# that changes shape depending on which OS checked it out is not a baseline.
UI/WebUI/tools/webctl/baseline/**   -text
UI/WebUI/tools/webctl/fixtures/**   -text

# Golden inspection data, compared the same way.
InspectionCore/test_suite/qa/**     -text

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not run under sh/bash.
*.sh        text eol=lf

# Binary, so git never guesses.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.gz        binary
*.bmp       binary
*.hydef     -text
